From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:48:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(audio): preserve native PlaySound coordinate units

A controlled 1.26.51.1 capture on protocol 2193 sends (-33, 567, -18)
for a sound at (-4.125, 70.875, -2.25). Bedrock and Java both encode
PlaySound positions in eighths of a block. Preserve the signed integers
instead of multiplying them or converting through floating point.

Decode the full Bedrock payload into a typed value, including signed loop
counts and independent optional handle and playback-position fields.
These fields remain available for native playback integration; ordinary
Java playback still cannot reproduce server handle controls or loops.

Test fractional negative positions, integer limits, signed loops, optional
field combinations, and byte alignment of both protocol representations.
